# Benefits Section: Neumorphic Redesign

We will update the [Benefits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Benefits.tsx) component to implement a neumorphic (soft UI) effect on the benefit cards, giving them a high-end "integrated" look.

## Proposed Changes

### [Benefits Component]
#### [MODIFY] [Benefits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Benefits.tsx)
-   Implement dual shadow system (light highlight and dark shadow) to create the neumorphic effect.
-   Adjust background colors to harmonize with the soft UI aesthetic.
-   Add an "inset" effect on hover or active states to make cards feel like they are being pressed into the screen.
-   Ensure the design stays clean and doesn't conflict with the existing "Liquid Glass" theme elsewhere.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` to ensure no UI breakages.

### Manual Verification
- Visual inspection of the soft UI shadows on different screen sizes.
- Verify that the card looks "inside" the screen as requested.
